# Investigation: Logseq Custom CSS Customization System

**Date:** November 23, 2025  
**Investigator:** GitHub Copilot  
**Status:** Complete  
**Version:** Logseq v0.11.x+

---

## Executive Summary

### Key Findings

- ✅ **Custom CSS file location:** `logseq/custom.css` in both file-based and database graphs
- ✅ **Different paths for DB vs File-based graphs:** DB graphs use `~/logseq/graphs/<graph-name>/logseq/custom.css`
- ✅ **Hot-reload supported:** File watcher automatically reloads CSS on change
- ✅ **Two usage methods:** Direct custom.css file OR remote CSS URL via config
- ✅ **Asset link expansion:** Relative asset paths are automatically resolved

### Quick Reference

| Aspect          | File-Based Graph                | Database Graph                                   |
| --------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| **Path**        | `<graph-dir>/logseq/custom.css` | **Stored in database** (not filesystem)          |
| **Edit Via**    | Settings → Edit custom.css      | Settings → Edit custom.css (in-app editor)       |
| **Hot Reload**  | ✅ Yes (file watcher)           | ✅ Yes (database change detection)               |
| **Alternative** | `:custom-css-url` in config.edn | `:custom-css-url` in config.edn                  |

---

## 1. Technical Deep Dive

### 1.1 File Path Resolution

**Location:** `src/main/frontend/config.cljs:452-459`

```clojure
(defn get-custom-css-path
  ([]
   (get-custom-css-path (state/get-current-repo)))
  ([repo]
   (if (db-based-graph? repo)
     (path/path-join app-name custom-css-file)          ;; "logseq/custom.css"
     (when-let [repo-dir (get-repo-dir repo)]
       (path/path-join repo-dir app-name custom-css-file)))))
```

#### Path Construction Logic

**For DB-based graphs:**

**IMPORTANT:** Database graphs do **NOT** store `custom.css` on the filesystem!

Instead:
- ✅ `custom.css` is stored **IN the SQLite database**
- ✅ `:file/path` = `"logseq/custom.css"` (virtual path in database)
- ✅ Content stored in `:file/content` attribute
- ❌ NO physical file at `~/logseq/graphs/<graph-name>/logseq/custom.css`

**How it works:**
1. Graph created → `custom.css` entity inserted into database (create_graph.cljs:201-205)
2. User edits via Settings → Saves to database
3. CSS loaded via `db/get-file repo "logseq/custom.css"` → retrieves from database
4. Changes persist in SQLite + transit exports

**Why filesystem paths don't work:**
- `~/logseq/graphs/<graph-name>/` contains only the SQLite `.db` file
- Creating `custom.css` file there won't work - Logseq reads from database, not filesystem

**Verification:**
```clojure
;; Database entity (deps/db/src/logseq/db/sqlite/create_graph.cljs:201-205)
{:block/uuid (gen-uuid "logseq/custom.css")
 :file/path "logseq/custom.css"      ;; Virtual path
 :file/content ""                     ;; Actual CSS content
 :file/created-at (js/Date.)
 :file/last-modified-at (js/Date.)}
```
```

**For File-based graphs:**

```
<graph-root-directory>/logseq/custom.css
```

### 1.2 CSS Loading Mechanism

**Entry Point:** `src/main/frontend/handler/ui.cljs:111-125`

```clojure
(defn add-style-if-exists!
  []
  (when-let [style (or (state/get-custom-css-link)      ;; 1. Check for URL override
                       (db-model/get-custom-css))]      ;; 2. Read custom.css file
    (if (config/db-based-graph? (state/get-current-repo))
      (p/let [style (assets-handler/<expand-assets-links-for-db-graph style)]
        (util/add-style! style))
      (some-> (config/expand-relative-assets-path style)
              (util/add-style!)))))

(defn reset-custom-css!
  []
  (when-let [el-style (gdom/getElement "logseq-custom-theme-id")]
    (dom/remove! el-style))
  (add-style-if-exists!))
```

#### Load Priority

1. **`:custom-css-url`** from `config.edn` (if set) - **HIGHEST PRIORITY**
2. **`logseq/custom.css`** file content (fallback)

### 1.3 File Retrieval

**Location:** `src/main/frontend/db/model.cljs:57-60`

```clojure
(defn get-custom-css
  []
  (when-let [repo (state/get-current-repo)]
    (get-file repo "logseq/custom.css")))
```

This retrieves the file content from the database (both file-based and DB graphs store file metadata in DataScript).

### 1.4 Hot Reload (File Watcher)

**Location:** `src/main/frontend/fs/watcher_handler.cljs:118-123`

```clojure
(and (contains? #{"add" "change" "unlink"} type)
     (string/ends-with? path "logseq/custom.css"))
(do
  (println "reloading custom.css")
  (ui-handler/add-style-if-exists!))
```

#### File Watcher Events

| Event    | Action                   |
| -------- | ------------------------ |
| `add`    | Load custom.css          |
| `change` | Reload custom.css        |
| `unlink` | Remove custom.css styles |

**Timeline:**

```
File change detected → watcher_handler receives event → reset-custom-css! called
   [~0ms]              [~10-50ms]                        [~100ms]
```

### 1.5 Asset Path Resolution

**Location:** `src/main/frontend/config.cljs:468-480`

```clojure
(defn expand-relative-assets-path
  "Resolve all relative links in custom.css to assets:// URL"
  ;; ../assets/xxx -> {assets|file}://{current-graph-root-path}/xxx
  [source]
  (when-not (string/blank? source)
    (let [protocol (and (string? source)
                        (not (string/blank? source))
                        (if (util/electron?) "assets://" "file://"))
          ;; BUG: use "assets" as fake current directory
          assets-link-fn (fn [_]
                           (let [graph-root (get-repo-dir (state/get-current-repo))
                                 full-path (if (util/safe-re-find #"^(file|assets):" graph-root)
                                             (path/path-join graph-root "assets")
                                             ...
```

**Transformation:**

```css
/* Before (in custom.css) */
background-image: url('../assets/background.png');

/* After expansion */
background-image: url('assets:///path/to/graph/assets/background.png');
```

---

## 2. Flow Diagrams

### 2.1 CSS Loading Flow

```
User opens graph
    ↓
Component theme.cljs mounts (hooks/use-effect!)
    ↓
ui-handler/reset-custom-css! called
    ↓
    ├─→ Remove existing <style id="logseq-custom-theme-id">
    └─→ add-style-if-exists!
         ↓
         ├─→ Check state/get-custom-css-link (from config :custom-css-url)
         │   └─→ If exists, use remote URL
         └─→ Fallback: db-model/get-custom-css
             └─→ db/get-file "logseq/custom.css"
                 ↓
                 ├─→ [DB Graph] Expand asset links for DB
                 └─→ [File Graph] Expand relative asset paths
                     ↓
                     util/add-style! (inject <style> element)
                         ↓
                     CSS applied to page
```

### 2.2 Hot Reload Flow

```
User edits custom.css file
    ↓
File system detects change [~0ms]
    ↓
fs/watcher emits "change" event [~10-50ms]
    ↓
watcher_handler checks path ends with "logseq/custom.css" [~60ms]
    ↓
ui-handler/add-style-if-exists! called [~100ms]
    ↓
Old styles removed, new styles injected [~150ms]
    ↓
Browser re-renders with new CSS [~200-300ms]
```

**Total reload time:** ~200-300ms

### 2.3 Settings UI Flow

```
User clicks Settings → Custom Theme → "Edit custom.css"
    ↓
settings.cljs/edit-custom-css renders button
    ↓
config/get-custom-css-path resolves path
    │
    ├─→ [DB Graph] "logseq/custom.css"
    └─→ [File Graph] "<repo-dir>/logseq/custom.css"
        ↓
rfe/href :file navigates to file editor
    ↓
User edits in Logseq's file editor
    ↓
File saved → triggers watcher → hot reload
```

---

