## 4. Usage Guide

### 4.1 Method 1: Direct custom.css File (Recommended)

#### For File-Based Graphs

**Step 1:** Navigate to Settings

```text
Click ⚙️ (gear icon) → Settings → General
```

**Step 2:** Click "Edit custom.css"

```text
Settings → General → Custom Theme → [Edit custom.css]
```

**Step 3:** Edit and save

```css
/* Example: Change accent color */
:root {
  --lx-accent-09: #ff6b6b;
}
```

**Alternative:** Edit directly in filesystem

```bash
# Navigate to your graph directory
cd /path/to/your/graph

# Edit the file
nano logseq/custom.css
# OR
code logseq/custom.css
```

**Hot Reload:** Changes auto-apply on save (file watcher detects changes)

---

#### For Database Graphs

**IMPORTANT:** Database graphs store `custom.css` **inside the SQLite database**, not as a filesystem file.

**Step 1:** Navigate to Settings

```text
Click ⚙️ (gear icon) → Settings → General
```

**Step 2:** Click "Edit custom.css"

```text
Settings → General → Custom Theme → [Edit custom.css]
```

**Step 3:** Edit in the in-app editor and save

```css
/* Example: Change accent color */
:root {
  --lx-accent-09: #ff6b6b;
}
```

**CRITICAL NOTES:**

- ❌ **Cannot edit via external text editor** (no filesystem file exists)
- ❌ Creating `~/logseq/graphs/<graph-name>/logseq/custom.css` **will NOT work**
- ✅ **Must use Logseq's built-in editor** (Settings → Edit custom.css)
- ✅ Changes persist in database and transit exports
- ✅ Hot reload still works (database change detection)

**Why no filesystem access?**

Database graphs store everything in SQLite:

```bash
# What actually exists on disk:
~/logseq/graphs/my-graph/
  └── my-graph.db           # SQLite database containing everything
  
# custom.css is INSIDE this database file, not as a separate file
```

/* Style specific components */
.block-content {
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.8;
}
```

**File location:**

```
<your-graph-folder>/logseq/custom.css
```

#### For Database Graphs

**Step 1-3:** Same as file-based

**File location:**

```
macOS:    ~/logseq/graphs/<graph-name>/logseq/custom.css
Windows:  %USERPROFILE%\logseq\graphs\<graph-name>\logseq\custom.css
Linux:    ~/.logseq/graphs/<graph-name>/logseq/custom.css
```

**Example full paths:**

**macOS:**

```
/Users/john/logseq/graphs/MyNotes/logseq/custom.css
```

**Windows:**

```
C:\Users\John\logseq\graphs\MyNotes\logseq\custom.css
```

**Linux:**

```
/home/john/.logseq/graphs/MyNotes/logseq/custom.css
```

### 4.2 Method 2: Remote CSS URL

**Location:** `logseq/config.edn`

```clojure
{
 ;; ...other config...

 ;; Specify a custom CSS import.
 ;; This option takes precedence over the local `logseq/custom.css` file.
 :custom-css-url "@import url('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/dracula/logseq@master/custom.css');"
}
```

**Priority:**

```
:custom-css-url > local custom.css
```

If `:custom-css-url` is set, the local `custom.css` file is **ignored**.

### 4.3 Using Asset References

#### Relative Paths (Recommended)

```css
/* In custom.css */
.my-custom-bg {
  background-image: url('../assets/background.png');
}
```

This gets auto-expanded to:

```css
.my-custom-bg {
  background-image: url('assets:///path/to/graph/assets/background.png');
}
```

#### Asset Structure

**File-based graph:**

```
graph-folder/
├── logseq/
│   ├── config.edn
│   └── custom.css
├── assets/
│   ├── background.png
│   └── logo.svg
└── pages/
```

**Database graph:**

```
~/logseq/graphs/MyGraph/
├── logseq/
│   ├── config.edn
│   └── custom.css
└── assets/
    ├── background.png
    └── logo.svg
```

---

## 5. Comparison: File-Based vs Database Graphs

### 5.1 Path Differences

| Aspect            | File-Based                      | Database                                   |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| **Base Location** | User-chosen directory           | `~/logseq/graphs/<name>/`                  |
| **Full Path**     | `<graph-dir>/logseq/custom.css` | `~/logseq/graphs/<name>/logseq/custom.css` |
| **Portability**   | ✅ Moves with folder            | ❌ Fixed to home directory                 |
| **Sync**          | ✅ Via Git/Dropbox              | ⚠️ Requires file sync of home dir          |

### 5.2 Behavior Differences

| Feature                 | File-Based             | Database                | Notes                 |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------- |
| **Hot Reload**          | ✅ Yes                 | ✅ Yes                  | Same watcher          |
| **Asset Links**         | Expanded to `file://`  | Expanded to `assets://` | Different protocols   |
| **Edit in Settings**    | ✅ Yes                 | ✅ Yes                  | Same UI               |
| **Remote URL Override** | ✅ Yes                 | ✅ Yes                  | Via `:custom-css-url` |
| **File Storage**        | File system + DB cache | File system + SQLite    | Both persist to disk  |

### 5.3 Asset Resolution Differences

**File-Based:**

```clojure
;; Protocol: file://
(if (util/electron?) "assets://" "file://")
```

**Database:**

```clojure
;; Uses assets-handler/<expand-assets-links-for-db-graph
;; Protocol: assets:// (Electron) or memory:// (web)
```

---

## 6. Advanced Scenarios

### 6.1 Theme Plugin vs Custom CSS

| Method                | Use Case               | Distribution | Complexity |
| --------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------ | ---------- |
| **custom.css**        | Personal customization | Manual copy  | Low        |
| **Plugin Theme**      | Shareable themes       | Marketplace  | Medium     |
| **`:custom-css-url`** | Team-wide theme        | CDN URL      | Low        |

### 6.2 Multiple Graphs

Each graph has **independent** custom.css:

```
~/logseq/graphs/
├── Work/
│   └── logseq/
│       └── custom.css    (work theme)
├── Personal/
│   └── logseq/
│       └── custom.css    (personal theme)
└── Research/
    └── logseq/
        └── custom.css    (reading theme)
```

### 6.3 CSS Injection Order

```html
<head>
  <!-- 1. Built-in Logseq styles -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="static/css/style.css" />

  <!-- 2. Plugin themes (if any) -->
  <style data-plugin-theme="...">
    ...
  </style>

  <!-- 3. Custom CSS (HIGHEST SPECIFICITY) -->
  <style id="logseq-custom-theme-id">
    /* Your custom.css content */
  </style>
</head>
```

**Precedence:** Custom CSS > Plugin themes > Built-in styles

---

## 7. Troubleshooting

### 7.1 CSS Not Loading

**Symptoms:** Changes to custom.css don't appear

**Checklist:**

1. ✅ Verify file path is correct

   ```bash
   # File-based
   ls "<graph-dir>/logseq/custom.css"

   # Database
   ls "~/logseq/graphs/<graph-name>/logseq/custom.css"
   ```

2. ✅ Check for `:custom-css-url` override in `config.edn`

   ```clojure
   ;; If this is set, local custom.css is ignored!
   :custom-css-url "..."
   ```

3. ✅ Verify CSS syntax is valid

   ```bash
   # Use a CSS validator or browser dev tools
   ```

4. ✅ Check browser DevTools Console for errors

   ```javascript
   // Look for CSS parsing errors
   ```

5. ✅ Confirm file watcher is running
   ```
   Edit custom.css → Save → Should see "reloading custom.css" in console
   ```

### 7.2 Asset Links Broken

**Symptoms:** Background images or fonts don't load

**Solution:**

```css
/* ❌ Wrong - Absolute path */
background: url('/assets/bg.png');

/* ❌ Wrong - Wrong relative depth */
background: url('assets/bg.png');

/* ✅ Correct - Relative from logseq/ to assets/ */
background: url('../assets/bg.png');
```

**File structure reminder:**

```
graph/
├── logseq/custom.css  ← You are here
└── assets/bg.png      ← Target (one level up, then into assets/)
```

### 7.3 Styles Not Overriding

**Cause:** CSS specificity too low

**Solutions:**

```css
/* ❌ Low specificity */
.block {
  color: red;
}

/* ✅ Higher specificity */
#app-container .block-content {
  color: red !important;
}

/* ✅ Alternative: Use :root variables */
:root {
  --ls-primary-text-color: #ff0000;
}
```

### 7.4 Hot Reload Not Working

**Diagnosis:**

1. Check file watcher is enabled (Electron only)
2. Manually reload: Settings → Re-index
3. Restart Logseq

**Manual reload:**

```javascript
// Browser console (web version)
logseq.api.reloadTheme()
```

